1672. Richest Customer Wealth

Description:
Given a 2D array accounts, where each row represents a customer and each value represents the money they have in a bank, find the maximum total wealth of any customer.

Test Case:

Input:  accounts = [[1,2,3],[3,2,1]]
Output: 6

Why?

Customer 1 → 1 + 2 + 3 = 6
Customer 2 → 3 + 2 + 1 = 6

The maximum wealth is 6.

class Solution {
    public int maximumWealth(int[][] accounts) {
        int max=0,sum=0;
        for(int i=0;i<accounts.length;i++){
            sum=0;
            for(int j=0;j<accounts[i].length;j++){
                sum+=accounts[i][j];
                if(sum>max){
                    max=sum;
                }
            }
            
        }
        return max;
    }
}
